HISTORICAL — applied in WP05; kept for the record.

WP05 activation contract: the three activation-scoped mission type reads, saved from WP02.

WP02 first declared getActivationMissionType, getActivationMissionStep and getActivationMissionSkeleton as
x-reserved (contract set activation, #99) with a 501. The coordinator ruled that they are declared when they
are built, in the same PR, so nothing is ever reserved. This patch holds what WP05 re-adds. The x-reserved
markers, the 501 responses and the "reserved / no link points here" wording are already DROPPED from it,
so the operations go in as built operations.

Apply from the repository root, on top of WP02 (and WP03/WP04):  git apply <this file>
It adds:
- paths/activations_activationId_artifacts_mission_type_missionTypeId[_steps_stepId|_skeletons_skeletonName].yaml
- the three openapi.yaml path entries, and "and of an activation" in the MissionTypes tag description
- examples Artifact.activation-mission-type.yaml, MissionStep.activation-implement.yaml,
  MissionSkeleton.activation-spec-template.yaml and their examples/_index.yaml entries
- responses/ActivationMissionTypeNotFound.yaml and its responses/_index.yaml entry
- the activation operations in CharterRefusalCode.yaml's raised-by text of mission_type_not_found/action_not_found

The CharterRefusalCode qualification of "No operation of the activation set is reserved any more" is not
carried: it existed only to name the reservation, and with no reservation that sentence stays as on main.
Notes for WP05:
- ActivationMissionTypeNotFound.yaml's example names skeleton_not_found; :contracts:checkRefusalExamples
  accepts it only once x-refusal says raised: true (WP04 flips it).
- MissionStep.activation-implement.yaml links /activations/a-1/artifacts/mission_step_contract/implement,
  the generic activation item read of the profiles mission.
- Add a ### Added change fragment for the three operations and the scenarios that cover their 200s.

